@* Facebook/Instagram/Messenger in-app browsers can block the native file chooser used for
   the screenshot upload below, showing an OS toast like "Please allow all media to use
   file chooser" instead of opening the picker. Detect via UA and nudge the user to open
   this page in their real browser. *@
<div id="inAppBrowserWarning" class="alert alert-warning d-none mb-3" role="alert">
    <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle-fill me-1"></i>
    <strong>Can't open the file picker?</strong> You're viewing this inside the Facebook/Instagram app browser,
    which can block photo uploads. Tap the <strong>&#8942; (or &bull;&bull;&bull;)</strong> menu at the top
    and choose <strong>&quot;Open in Browser&quot;</strong> (Chrome/Safari), then try uploading again.
</div>
<script>
    (function () {
        var ua = navigator.userAgent || '';
        if (/FBAN|FBAV|FB_IAB|Instagram|Line\//i.test(ua)) {
            document.getElementById('inAppBrowserWarning')?.classList.remove('d-none');
        }
    })();
</script>
